# WT-3-prod-multidevice — Linux headless server device template.
#
# This device runs the observer (:18091) + slave-A daemon (:18093).
# Same shape as the prod-runbook host-mode observer/slave-A, but
# now on a distinct physical device from the driver.
#
# HARNESS-ONLY: oauth_placeholder MUST stay literal.

kind: device
role: observer,slave-a
device_kind: headless
listen: 127.0.0.1:18091
oauth_placeholder: <OAUTH_TOKEN_HERE_DO_NOT_COMMIT>
notes: |
  Runs two daemons: observer on :18091, slave-A on :18093. Both
  bind loopback only — cross-device traffic goes through agentserver
  -signed tunnels (never hardcoded here). Same OAuth token as driver
  is used for daemon-link WS handshake with observer via workspace_id.
